      {
        "id": 39185,
        "name": "TheJayMann",
        "username": "TheJayMann",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/{size}/2261_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-09-24T21:30:06.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Well, if you want to think of it as multiple steps, with all those cards out, he has a status effect of cold damage +2, fire damage -1.&nbsp; Every time he initiates an attack, the necessary modifiers are applied.&nbsp; So, more or less, he could read a modified power of \"deals himself 3 cold or 0 fire damage,\" yes.&nbsp; But, if you initiate cold damage, it would be 1 + 2 cold damage, but if something converted that cold damage to fire damage, the cold damage modifier goes away and the fire damage modifier applies, making it 1 - 1 fire damage.&nbsp; Given that modifiers will keep changing while other cards modify damage types and redirect damage, it's simpler to wait until you are at a point of final damage before applying count modifiers.</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
